# .dockerignore for the build-docker.yml image build (context: the repo root).
#
# distro/Dockerfile only COPYs from distro/ (the vacti-engine-chromium .debs arrive
# via the SEPARATE `engine_debs` named build-context, which this file does not touch),
# so everything else in the repo is transfer-only bloat. Ignore all, then re-include
# exactly what the build reads. This drops .git (~6.4 MB), the connector Go module, the
# CI/HF/scripts trees and the staged engine-debs/ from the context the daemon receives.
*

# What distro/Dockerfile actually needs.
!distro/

# Belt-and-braces: never let VCS metadata, dependency trees, or large disk images ride
# in even from a re-included path.
**/.git
**/.github
**/node_modules
engine-debs/
**/*.deb
**/*.ova
**/*.qcow2
**/*.vmdk
**/*.iso
